## 7. Feature-Level Target State

AgentMesh should be a policy-enforced trust fabric. Handshakes should be signed, replay-safe, audience-bound, and backed by trusted agent identities. Mesh messages and handoffs should be evaluated server-side using identity, lifecycle, trust score, policy, environment, and rate limits. Trust scores should use one versioned schema with explainability. Revocation/quarantine should immediately block mesh operations and invalidate trust cards. SDKs should expose the same trust contracts rather than separate MVP surfaces. Tests should cover replay, revocation, server-side policy decisions, schema consistency, and audit evidence.
